Mutation testing for Rust and Cargo.

rust-mutants copies the workspace into a disposable snapshot, instruments every compilable mutant of
the selected files once, builds the test binaries once, and activates one mutant per test process
through an environment variable. The source workspace is never modified.

Usage: rust-mutants <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list         List the candidates the rules propose, before the compiler has ruled
  catalog      Catalog the mutants the compiler accepts, and the candidates it refused with its own
               words
  run          Run one mutant and report what the tests said
  explain      Say everything known about one mutant
  instrument   Print one file as the engine rewrites it, guards and runtime included
  why-skipped  Tally why places were passed over
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
